==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|testifien}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|testifier}}, from {{der|en|la|testificārī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|testificor||I bear witness}}, from {{m|la|testis||a witness}} + {{m|la|facere||to make}}. See {{af|en|-fy}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|testif|ies}} {{tcx|en|ambitransitive}}

# To make a [[declaration]], or give [[evidence]], under [[oath]].
#* '''2014''', {{w|Ruzwana Bashir}}, "[http://www.theguardian.com/society/2014/aug/29/-sp-untold-story-culture-of-shame-ruzwana-bashir The untold story of how a culture of shame perpetuates abuse. I know, I was a victim]", ''The Guardian'', 29 August 2014:
#*: It was only after a decade away from Skipton that I was finally able to garner the courage to return and '''testify''' against my abuser.
#* Bible, Numbers xxxv. 30
#*: One witness shall not '''testify''' against any person to cause him to die.
# To make a [[statement]] based on [[personal]] [[knowledge]] or [[faith]].
#* Bible, John iii. 11
#*: We speak that we do know, and '''testify''' that we have seen; and ye receive not our witness.

